{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Even in your knowledge.</b> Even though the king is a youth, guard yourself lest you curse him even in your knowledge — its meaning is in your heart and in your thoughts, which you alone know. And in a hidden place, do not curse the rich, for if the king hears he will harm you by his power, and the rich by his wealth." "<b>For a bird of the heavens.</b> By way of parable, like 'for it hears everything' [Ecclesiastes 7:7 according to some readings; or: for a thing hears everything]." "<b>And the possessor of wings.</b> It is 'a bird of the heavens,' and the matter is doubled."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:04.169192611Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}